<BaseLayout title="Employee Onboarding & Identity Service | Amit Madakatti" description="An AWS employee onboarding workflow combining Cognito identity, Step Functions orchestration, Lambda APIs and S3 document handling.">
<main class="case-page"><a class="back-link" href="/work/">← ALL WORK</a><span class="eyebrow">CASE 02 / CLOUD ENGINEERING / 2026</span><h1>Smart employee<br/><em>onboarding.</em></h1><p class="case-lead">An event-driven employee onboarding and identity workflow built around AWS managed services.</p><div class="case-cover cover-blue"><div class="architecture-nodes"><span>API GATEWAY</span><i>→</i><span>LAMBDA</span><i>→</i><span>STEP FUNCTIONS</span><i>→</i><span>DYNAMODB</span></div></div><div class="case-meta"><div><span>ROLE</span><b>Cloud Engineering / Team project</b></div><div><span>STACK</span><b>Lambda · Cognito · Step Functions · DynamoDB · SES · S3</b></div><div><span>YEAR</span><b>2026</b></div></div><div class="case-content"><section><span class="eyebrow">01 / THE BRIEF</span><h2>Make onboarding<br/><em>less manual.</em></h2><p>Design a secure employee onboarding workflow that connects identity, workflow orchestration, notifications and employee records.</p></section><section><span class="eyebrow">02 / THE BUILD</span><h2>Managed services,<br/>clear boundaries.</h2><p>The solution uses API Gateway and Lambda for APIs, Cognito for identity, Step Functions for orchestration, DynamoDB for records, SES for email and S3 for documents. Work was split across service ownership with defined IAM boundaries.</p></section><section><span class="eyebrow">03 / STATUS</span><h2>Built with a team.</h2><p>Implemented the identity, workflow and API work packages. Full end-to-end deployment and final integration evidence are still being consolidated.</p><p>The work completed on my side covers identity services, workflow orchestration and the API layer. The wider project also includes document and portal work owned by other contributors, so this case study distinguishes my implementation scope from the overall system.</p></section><section><span class="eyebrow">04 / INTEGRATION &amp; VALIDATION</span><h2>Contracts before<br/><em>end-to-end claims.</em></h2><p>The workflow uses Step Functions to coordinate onboarding stages, with Lambda handlers and callback paths forming the integration boundary. Cognito provides the identity layer; DynamoDB stores onboarding records; S3 handles document storage; and SES supports email notifications.</p><p>Unit tests for the identity and workflow services passed during development, and the API work package was integrated. Full end-to-end deployment and final integration evidence remain outstanding, so this project is presented as an implementation in progress rather than a production-proven service.</p></section></div><a class="case-repo" href="https://github.com/amit-cloudops-ai/hrms-onboarding-service" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">VIEW SOURCE REPOSITORY ↗</a></main>
</BaseLayout>
